{
  "about": "The play_passage matcher's cases (narai.tools.music_match.match; 2026-10-31: Narai owns music.* and play_passage). Narai's judge and the SDK's matcher (a tool's preview) both run every case and must agree. A played note's time is at_ms - latency_ms; each expected note, in time order, takes the earliest unused played note within timing_ms and pitch_tolerance semitones (pitches are MIDI numbers, as music.played@1 carries them). A note with no pitch (a rhythm's onset, a tap) matches on time alone. Outcomes per expected note: hit, wrong_pitch (a note in its window, another pitch), early or late (its pitch, outside the window), missed. extras: played notes no expected note took. An expected note with no at_ms is untimed (a one-note target): every played note is in its window, so it is a hit, wrong_pitch or missed, never early or late. A case with \"ordered\": true is an ordered passage (no at_ms): each expected note, in the key's order, takes the earliest unused played note of its pitch after the previous one taken (a hit), at any time; a note left open takes the earliest unused played note between its neighbours' (a wrong_pitch), else it is missed. Never early or late.",
